{"message": "Fixed the defect in `/zephyrproject/zephyr/kernel/usage.c` where enabling or disabling thread runtime stats on the currently running thread did not properly update the CPU's `usage0` cycle timestamp:

- In `k_thread_runtime_stats_disable()`, when `thread == cpu->current`, updated `cpu->usage0 = now` after crediting the elapsed cycles to the thread and CPU so that subsequent cycle updates do not double-count the elapsed time.
- In `k_thread_runtime_stats_enable()`, when `thread == cpu->current`, flushed the elapsed cycles since `cpu->usage0` to the CPU stats (`sched_cpu_update_usage`) and advanced `cpu->usage0 = now` so that cycles executed while thread tracking was disabled are not credited to the thread after re-enabling.", "kind": "FinishAction"}

